---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Native vs WASM image encoder benchmark — PixKeep Lab"
  description="How good is the image encoder built into your browser? canvas.toBlob JPEG / WebP / AVIF at six quality levels, measured against WASM reference encoders (MozJPEG, libwebp, @jsquash-avif): byte sizes, encode latency, DSSIM quality. Everything runs locally."
>
  <h1>Native vs WASM image encoder benchmark</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    How good is the image encoder built into <em>your</em> browser? Pick some photos,
    or use our reference images. This page encodes them with your browser's built-in
    image encoder — <code>canvas.toBlob()</code> — in three formats (JPEG, WebP, AVIF),
    six quality levels each. Then it encodes the same pixels again with the
    <strong>reference encoders</strong> compiled to WASM (MozJPEG, libwebp, libavif),
    so you can compare your browser against known-good implementations.
    You get output bytes, encode latency and DSSIM quality for both paths, measured on
    your machine and your browser version. Nothing is uploaded; your photos never leave
    this page.
  </p>

  <div class="card" id="env-card">
    <h2>Your environment</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0">
      Encoders are native code inside your browser/engine, so the numbers below are a
      property of <em>this exact setup</em> — browser, version, OS, CPU/GPU all move them.
      Read locally; only shared if you choose to share.
    </p>
    <dl id="env-list" class="env-grid"><dt>Status</dt><dd>collecting…</dd></dl>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>1 · Choose images</h2>
    <div class="pick">
      <div>
        <h3>Your photos</h3>
        <p class="muted">Best signal — real content at real resolutions. PNG/JPEG/WebP/AVIF, whatever your browser can decode.</p>
        <input type="file" id="files" multiple accept="image/*" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Reference images <span class="muted">(served from cdn.pixkeep.app)</span></h3>
        <p class="muted">The same four images our published numbers use — comparable across devices.</p>
        <div id="samples"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>2 · Run</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Full resolution is timed as median of 3 runs. Quality is scored as DSSIM against a
      center-square crop of the source (capped at
      1200px — the same framing for every encode, so native and WASM paths compare equal). A full pass
      on 12MP photos takes several minutes — 20+ in Safari (JPEG-only is much quicker).
      <strong>Keep this tab in the foreground</strong> (background tabs get throttled and
      pollute the timings).
    </p>
    <p class="run-row">
      <button class="btn" id="run" disabled>Run benchmark</button>
      <span class="fmt-pick">
        Formats:
        <label><input type="checkbox" class="fmt" value="jpeg" checked /> JPEG</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" class="fmt" value="webp" /> WebP</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" class="fmt" value="avif" /> AVIF <span class="muted">(WASM-only; minutes-scale on 12MP)</span></label>
      </span>
    </p>
    <div class="progress"><div id="progress-bar"></div></div>
    <pre id="status">idle</pre>
  </div>

  <div id="results"></div>

  <div class="card" id="share-card" hidden>
    <h2>3 · Share your run (optional)</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Different device? Different browser? Your run helps map the matrix — especially
      Safari, Firefox on Linux, and mobile. The JSON contains only the numbers and the
      environment block above; no image data, nothing else.
    </p>
    <p class="share-row">
      <button class="btn" id="download">Download JSON</button>
      <button class="btn ghost" id="copy">Copy summary</button>
      <a class="btn ghost" id="email" href="#">Email to dev@pixkeep.app</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/pixkeep/lab/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Post on GitHub Discussions</a>
    </p>
    <p class="muted" id="copy-note"></p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Methodology &amp; caveats</h2>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Quality scales are not comparable across encoders.</strong> "q80" in Chromium's JPEG encoder, MozJPEG and libwebp are three different points on three curves. Compare formats at matched DSSIM, not matched q.</li>
      <li><strong>Support is detected by the returned blob's type</strong> — browsers that can't encode a format silently return PNG instead of throwing.</li>
      <li><strong>WASM reference encoders:</strong> MozJPEG (<code>@wasm-codecs/mozjpeg</code>), libwebp (<code>@jsquash/webp</code>), AVIF (<code>@jsquash/avif</code>) — encoded on the <em>same</em> analysis frame as native (identical DSSIM framing), plus one full-res timing run at q60 per format.</li>
      <li>Full resolution is timed as median of 3 runs. Quality is scored as DSSIM against a center-square crop of the source (capped at 1200px — same framing for every encode).</li>
      <li>Timings: median of 3 full-resolution encodes, warm JIT. DevTools closed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Found something odd? <a href="https://github.com/pixkeep/lab/discussions">Bring it to Discussions</a> — reproducible oddities become blog posts.</p>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    /* is:global — these rules target JS-created nodes, which never receive
       Astro's scoped-style attributes (scoped selectors silently miss them). */
    .env-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr; gap: 4px 16px; margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .env-grid dt { color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .env-grid dd { margin: 0; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .pick { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    @media (max-width: 760px) { .pick { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .pick h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 1rem; }
    #samples { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; }
    #samples .sample { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 0; padding: 6px 10px 6px 6px; cursor: pointer; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; background: #fff; transition: border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s; }
    #samples .sample:hover { border-color: #b9c6d4; }
    #samples .sample input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
    #samples .sample img { width: 48px; height: 48px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px; display: block; }
    #samples .sample-name { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.82rem; }
    #samples .sample-tip { position: absolute; left: 0; top: calc(100% + 6px); z-index: 5; background: rgba(12, 25, 41, 0.94); color: #dbe7f5; font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.35; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 8px; white-space: nowrap; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.15s; pointer-events: none; }
    #samples .sample:hover .sample-tip, #samples .sample:focus-within .sample-tip { opacity: 1; }
    #samples .sample:focus-within { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
    #samples .sample:has(input:checked) { border-color: var(--accent-deep); background: #eef4fd; }
    #samples .sample::after { content: '✓'; position: absolute; left: 44px; top: 1px; width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-size: 11px; display: grid; place-items: center; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.15s; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #fff; }
    #samples .sample:has(input:checked)::after { opacity: 1; }
    .run-row { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; }
    .fmt-pick { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 14px; font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .fmt-pick label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; margin: 0; }
    .progress { height: 8px; background: #e5eaf1; border-radius: 999px; overflow: hidden; margin: 12px 0 8px; }
    #progress-bar { height: 100%; width: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-deep), var(--accent)); transition: width 0.3s; }
    #status { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 0.85rem; background: var(--navy-0); color: #dbe7f5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; margin: 0; }
    .share-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
    .photo h3 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .fmt-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
    .fmt-head h4 { margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { computeDSSIM, loadImageFromBlob } from '../lib/dssim';
    import { encodeCanvasAsAvif, encodeCanvasAsJpeg, encodeCanvasAsWebp } from '../lib/encoders';
    import { collectDeviceInfo, enrichDeviceInfo } from '../lib/device-info';

    // ─── Config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const QUALITY_LEVELS = [10, 40, 60, 80, 92, 100];
    const FORMATS = [
      { key: 'jpeg', mime: 'image/jpeg', wasm: 'MozJPEG' },
      { key: 'webp', mime: 'image/webp', wasm: 'libwebp' },
      { key: 'avif', mime: 'image/avif', wasm: '@jsquash/avif' },
    ] as const;
    const REPS = 3;
    const ANALYSIS_SIZE = 1200;
    const CDN = 'https://cdn.pixkeep.app/bench-encode';
    const SAMPLES = [
      { key: 'flower1', desc: '12MP flower photo · 3024×4032', bytes: 22906732, thumb: 'flower1.jpg' },
      { key: 'grass1', desc: '12MP grass photo · 3024×4032', bytes: 24649588, thumb: 'grass1.jpg' },
      { key: 'graphic-text', desc: 'synthetic UI/text · 2400×1600', bytes: 113703, thumb: 'graphic-text.jpg' },
      { key: 'alpha-transparent', desc: 'RGBA transparency test · 2000×2000', bytes: 73705, thumb: 'alpha-transparent.png' },
    ];

    type Support = 'ok' | 'silent' | 'unsupported';
    interface Entry {
      group: 'native' | 'wasm'; format: string; q: number; support: Support;
      sizeFull?: number; msFull?: number; size1200?: number; dssim?: number;
      actualType?: string;
    }
    interface PhotoResult { file: string; source: string; width?: number; height?: number; entries: Entry[]; error?: string }

    // ─── DOM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const $ = <T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(sel: string) => document.querySelector(sel) as T;
    const statusEl = $('#status') as HTMLPreElement;
    const barEl = $('#progress-bar');
    const runBtn = $('#run') as HTMLButtonElement;
    const fileInput = $('#files') as HTMLInputElement;
    const resultsEl = $('#results');
    const status = (t: string) => { statusEl.textContent = t; };
    const progress = (frac: number) => { barEl.style.width = `${Math.round(frac * 100)}%`; };

    // ─── Environment card ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const deviceInfo = collectDeviceInfo();
    function renderEnv() {
      const rows: Array<[string, string]> = [
        ['Browser', `${deviceInfo.browser} ${deviceInfo.browserVersion} (${deviceInfo.engine})`],
        ['OS', deviceInfo.os + (deviceInfo.arch ? ` (${deviceInfo.arch})` : '')],
        ['CPU cores', deviceInfo.cores ? String(deviceInfo.cores) : 'not exposed'],
        ['Memory', deviceInfo.memoryGB != null ? `≈${deviceInfo.memoryGB} GB (browser-reported, may be rounded)` : 'not exposed by this browser'],
        ['GPU', deviceInfo.gpu ?? 'masked / not exposed'],
        ['Screen', deviceInfo.screen],
        ['Mobile', deviceInfo.mobile ? 'yes' : 'no'],
      ];
      $('#env-list').innerHTML = rows.map(([k, v]) => `<dt>${k}</dt><dd>${v}</dd>`).join('');
    }
    renderEnv();
    enrichDeviceInfo(deviceInfo).then(renderEnv);

    // ─── Sample picker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const samplesEl = $('#samples');
    for (const s of SAMPLES) {
      const label = document.createElement('label');
      label.className = 'sample';
      const meta = `${s.desc} · ${(s.bytes / 1048576).toFixed(1)} MB`;
      label.title = meta; // native tooltip fallback / a11y
      label.innerHTML = `
        <input type="checkbox" value="${s.key}" />
        <img src="/thumbs/${s.thumb}" alt="${s.key}" loading="lazy" />
        <span class="sample-name">${s.key}</span>
        <span class="sample-tip">${meta}</span>`;
      samplesEl.appendChild(label);
    }
    const selectedSamples = () =>
      [...samplesEl.querySelectorAll('input:checked')].map((i) => (i as HTMLInputElement).value);
    const fmtInputs = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('.fmt')];
    const selectedFormats = () => FORMATS.filter((f) => fmtInputs.some((i) => i.checked && i.value === f.key));
    function refreshRunBtn() {
      const hasImages = fileInput.files!.length > 0 || selectedSamples().length > 0;
      runBtn.disabled = !(hasImages && selectedFormats().length > 0);
    }
    fileInput.addEventListener('change', refreshRunBtn);
    samplesEl.addEventListener('change', refreshRunBtn);
    for (const i of fmtInputs) i.addEventListener('change', refreshRunBtn);

    // ─── Decode helpers (hardened — see repo history for the failure modes) ─
    async function fileToMemoryBlob(file: File): Promise<Blob> {
      let lastErr: unknown;
      for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
        try {
          return new Blob([await file.arrayBuffer()], { type: file.type });
        } catch (e) {
          lastErr = e;
          await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 400));
        }
      }
      throw lastErr;
    }
    async function blobToCanvas(blob: Blob): Promise<HTMLCanvasElement> {
      const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!;
      let bitmapErr: unknown = null;
      try {
        const bmp = await createImageBitmap(blob);
        canvas.width = bmp.width; canvas.height = bmp.height;
        ctx.drawImage(bmp, 0, 0);
        bmp.close();
        return canvas;
      } catch (e) { bitmapErr = e; }
      try {
        const img = await loadImageFromBlob(blob);
        canvas.width = img.naturalWidth; canvas.height = img.naturalHeight;
        ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0);
        return canvas;
      } catch (e) {
        throw new Error(`decode: bitmap[${(bitmapErr as Error)?.message || bitmapErr}] img[${(e as Error)?.message || e}]`);
      }
    }
    function toBlobP(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, mime: string, quality?: number): Promise<Blob | null> {
      return new Promise((resolve) => canvas.toBlob(resolve, mime, quality));
    }
    function median(xs: number[]): number {
      const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b);
      return s[Math.floor(s.length / 2)];
    }


    // Center-square cover-crop of the source, capped at ANALYSIS_SIZE — the
    // shared framing for every DSSIM comparison. Native encodes the full-res
    // frame (any aspect ratio), WASM encodes this same square; both are scored
    // against center squares of identical content, so DSSIM stays comparable
    // across source resolutions and aspect ratios.
    async function prepAnalysis(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): Promise<{ canvas: HTMLCanvasElement; ref: Blob }> {
      const side = Math.min(ANALYSIS_SIZE, canvas.width, canvas.height);
      const out = document.createElement('canvas');
      out.width = side;
      out.height = side;
      const ctx = out.getContext('2d')!;
      const w = canvas.width, h = canvas.height;
      const cropSide = Math.min(w, h);
      const sx = Math.floor((w - cropSide) / 2);
      const sy = Math.floor((h - cropSide) / 2);
      ctx.drawImage(canvas, sx, sy, cropSide, cropSide, 0, 0, side, side);
      const ref = await toBlobP(out, 'image/png');
      return { canvas: out, ref: ref! };
    }
    async function tryDssim(ref: Blob, blob: Blob): Promise<number | undefined> {
      try { return await computeDSSIM(ref, blob); } catch { return undefined; }
    }
    function wasmEncode(key: string, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, q: number): Promise<Blob> {
      if (key === 'webp') return encodeCanvasAsWebp(canvas, q, true);
      if (key === 'jpeg') return encodeCanvasAsJpeg(canvas, q, true);
      return encodeCanvasAsAvif(canvas, q);
    }

    // ─── Core run ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    async function runPhoto(name: string, source: string, canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, formats: readonly { key: string; mime: string }[], onStep: (s: string) => void): Promise<PhotoResult> {
      const entries: Entry[] = [];
      const { canvas: aCanvas, ref } = await prepAnalysis(canvas);

      for (const { key, mime } of formats) {
        const probe = await toBlobP(canvas, mime, 0.8);
        const support: Support = !probe ? 'unsupported' : probe.type !== mime ? 'silent' : 'ok';
        for (const q of QUALITY_LEVELS) {
          const entry: Entry = { group: 'native', format: key, q, support };
          if (support !== 'ok') {
            if (q === 80 && probe) { entry.sizeFull = probe.size; entry.actualType = probe.type; }
          } else {
            onStep(`native ${key} q${q}`);
            const times: number[] = [];
            let size = 0;
            for (let r = 0; r < REPS; r++) {
              const t0 = performance.now();
              const blob = await toBlobP(canvas, mime, q / 100);
              times.push(performance.now() - t0);
              size = blob!.size;
            }
            entry.sizeFull = size;
            entry.msFull = Math.round(median(times));
            const aBlob = await toBlobP(aCanvas, mime, q / 100);
            entry.size1200 = aBlob!.size;
            entry.dssim = await tryDssim(ref, aBlob!);
          }
          entries.push(entry);
        }
      }

      for (const { key } of formats) {
        for (const q of QUALITY_LEVELS) {
          onStep(`wasm ${key} q${q}`);
          const entry: Entry = { group: 'wasm', format: key, q, support: 'ok' };
          try {
            const aBlob = await wasmEncode(key, aCanvas, q / 100);
            entry.size1200 = aBlob.size;
            entry.dssim = await tryDssim(ref, aBlob);
          } catch (e) {
            entry.support = 'unsupported';
            entry.actualType = (e as Error)?.message || String(e);
          }
          entries.push(entry);
        }
        // Full-res WASM timing: single q60 run per format.
        onStep(`wasm ${key} full-res timing`);
        try {
          const t0 = performance.now();
          const blob = await wasmEncode(key, canvas, 0.6);
          const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - t0);
          const e60 = entries.find((en) => en.group === 'wasm' && en.format === key && en.q === 60);
          if (e60) { e60.sizeFull = blob.size; e60.msFull = ms; }
        } catch { /* timing is best-effort */ }
      }
      return { file: name, source, width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height, entries };
    }

    // ─── Rendering ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    const kb = (n?: number) => (n == null ? '—' : n >= 1048576 ? `${(n / 1048576).toFixed(2)} MB` : `${Math.round(n / 1024)} KB`);
    const ds = (n?: number) => (n == null ? '—' : n.toFixed(4));
    function badge(s: Support, actual?: string) {
      if (s === 'ok') return '<span class="badge ok">native ok</span>';
      if (s === 'silent') return `<span class="badge warn">silent → ${actual || 'PNG'}</span>`;
      return '<span class="badge bad">unsupported</span>';
    }
    function renderPhoto(r: PhotoResult) {
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'card photo';
      if (r.error) {
        card.innerHTML = `<h3>${r.file}</h3><p class="badge bad">failed</p><p class="muted">${r.error}</p>`;
        resultsEl.appendChild(card);
        return;
      }
      let html = `<h3>${r.file}</h3><p class="muted">${r.width}×${r.height} · source: ${r.source}</p>`;
      for (const { key, wasm } of FORMATS) {
        const nat = r.entries.filter((e) => e.group === 'native' && e.format === key);
        const support = nat.find((e) => e.q === 80)?.support ?? 'ok';
        const actual = nat.find((e) => e.q === 80)?.actualType;
        html += `<div class="fmt-head"><h4>${key.toUpperCase()}</h4>${badge(support, actual)}<span class="muted">WASM reference: ${wasm}</span></div>`;
        if (support !== 'ok') {
          const p80 = nat.find((e) => e.q === 80);
          html += `<p class="muted">native toBlob returned ${p80?.actualType ?? 'nothing'}${p80?.sizeFull ? ` (${kb(p80.sizeFull)})` : ''} for every quality level — see WASM column for what real ${key.toUpperCase()} encoding costs.</p>`;
        }
        html += `<table class="data"><thead><tr><th>q</th><th>native full-res</th><th>native time</th><th>native dssim</th><th>wasm size¹</th><th>wasm dssim</th></tr></thead><tbody>`;
        for (const q of QUALITY_LEVELS) {
          const n = nat.find((e) => e.q === q)!;
          const w = r.entries.find((e) => e.group === 'wasm' && e.format === key && e.q === q);
          html += `<tr><td>${q}</td><td>${support === 'ok' ? kb(n.sizeFull) : '—'}</td><td>${n.msFull != null ? `${n.msFull} ms` : '—'}</td><td>${support === 'ok' ? ds(n.dssim) : '—'}</td><td>${w ? kb(w.size1200) : '—'}</td><td>${w ? ds(w.dssim) : '—'}</td></tr>`;
        }
        html += '</tbody></table>';
      }
      card.innerHTML = html;
      resultsEl.appendChild(card);
    }

    // ─── Share ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    function setupShare(result: object) {
      ($('#share-card') as HTMLElement).hidden = false;
      const dl = $('#download') as HTMLButtonElement;
      dl.disabled = false;
      dl.onclick = () => {
        const blob = new Blob([JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)], { type: 'application/json' });
        const a = document.createElement('a');
        a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
        a.download = `encode-matrix-${deviceInfo.browser.toLowerCase()}-${new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.json`;
        a.click();
        URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href);
      };
      const summary = (result as { results: PhotoResult[] }).results.map((r) => {
        const line = (fmt: string) => {
          const e = r.entries.find((x) => x.group === 'native' && x.format === fmt && x.q === 80);
          if (!e) return `${fmt}: n/a`;
          return e.support === 'ok' ? `${fmt}@q80: ${kb(e.sizeFull)} in ${e.msFull}ms` : `${fmt}: ${e.support === 'silent' ? `silent→${e.actualType}` : 'unsupported'}`;
        };
        return `${r.file} (${r.width}×${r.height}): ${['jpeg', 'webp', 'avif'].map(line).join(' · ')}`;
      }).join('\n');
      const text = `Encode-matrix result — ${deviceInfo.browser} ${deviceInfo.browserVersion} (${deviceInfo.engine}) on ${deviceInfo.os}, ${deviceInfo.cores ?? '?'} cores, ${deviceInfo.gpu ?? 'GPU n/a'}\n${summary}`;
      ($('#copy') as HTMLButtonElement).onclick = async () => {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        $('#copy-note').textContent = 'Summary copied — the full JSON has the complete matrix (use Download).';
      };
      ($('#email') as HTMLAnchorElement).href =
        `mailto:dev@pixkeep.app?subject=${encodeURIComponent(`Encode-matrix result: ${deviceInfo.browser} on ${deviceInfo.os}`)}` +
        `&body=${encodeURIComponent(text + '\n\n(Full JSON attached / paste it here — Download JSON button.)')}`;
    }

    // ─── Orchestration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    async function collectSources(): Promise<Array<{ name: string; source: string; blob: Blob }>> {
      const out: Array<{ name: string; source: string; blob: Blob }> = [];
      for (const f of Array.from(fileInput.files || [])) {
        out.push({ name: f.name, source: 'local file', blob: await fileToMemoryBlob(f) });
      }
      for (const key of selectedSamples()) {
        const s = SAMPLES.find((x) => x.key === key)!;
        status(`fetching sample ${key} (${(s.bytes / 1048576).toFixed(1)} MB)…`);
        // Retry with backoff — CDN fetches occasionally die mid-handshake on
        // flaky networks (ERR_CONNECTION_CLOSED), and a 25 MB sample is worth
        // more than one attempt.
        let resp: Response | null = null;
        let lastErr: unknown;
        for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3 && !resp; attempt++) {
          try {
            const r = await fetch(`${CDN}/${key}.png`);
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);
            resp = r;
          } catch (e) {
            lastErr = e;
            status(`fetching sample ${key} — attempt ${attempt + 1} failed (${(e as Error)?.message || e}), retrying…`);
            await new Promise((r2) => setTimeout(r2, 1000 * (attempt + 1)));
          }
        }
        if (!resp) throw new Error(`sample fetch failed: ${key} (${(lastErr as Error)?.message || lastErr})`);
        out.push({ name: `${key}.png`, source: `${CDN}/${key}.png`, blob: await resp.blob() });
      }
      return out;
    }

    let running = false;
    async function run() {
      if (running) return;
      running = true;
      runBtn.disabled = true;
      resultsEl.innerHTML = '';
      const formats = selectedFormats();
      try {
        const sources = await collectSources();
        if (sources.length === 0) { status('no images selected'); return; }
        const results: PhotoResult[] = [];
        let stepCount = 0;
        const totalSteps = sources.length * formats.length * QUALITY_LEVELS.length * 2;
        for (let i = 0; i < sources.length; i++) {
          const s = sources[i];
          try {
            status(`[${i + 1}/${sources.length}] decoding ${s.name}…`);
            const canvas = await blobToCanvas(s.blob);
            const r = await runPhoto(s.name, s.source, canvas, formats, (step) => {
              stepCount++;
              progress(stepCount / totalSteps);
              status(`[${i + 1}/${sources.length}] ${s.name} — ${step}`);
            });
            results.push(r);
          } catch (e) {
            results.push({ file: s.name, source: s.source, entries: [], error: (e as Error)?.message || String(e) });
          }
          renderPhoto(results[results.length - 1]);
        }
        const result = { benchVersion: 1, generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(), device: deviceInfo, results };
        (window as any).__benchEncodeResult = result;
        status(`done: ${results.length} image(s), ${results.filter((r) => r.error).length} failed`);
        progress(1);
        setupShare(result);
      } catch (e) {
        status(`fatal: ${(e as Error)?.message || e}`);
      } finally {
        running = false;
        runBtn.disabled = false;
      }
    }
    runBtn.addEventListener('click', run);

    // ─── Automation hooks (Playwright) ─────────────────────────────────────
    // ?samples=all|flower1,grass1&autorun=1 — fetch reference images and run without
    // any user interaction; result lands in window.__benchEncodeResult.
    (window as any).__benchEncodeProgress = 'idle';
    const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    const sampleParam = params.get('samples');
    if (sampleParam) {
      const keys = sampleParam === 'all' ? SAMPLES.map((s) => s.key) : sampleParam.split(',').filter((k) => SAMPLES.some((s) => s.key === k));
      for (const box of samplesEl.querySelectorAll('input')) {
        (box as HTMLInputElement).checked = keys.includes((box as HTMLInputElement).value);
      }
      for (const i of fmtInputs) i.checked = true; // automation collects all formats
      refreshRunBtn();
      if (params.get('autorun') === '1') run();
    }
  </script>
</Base>
